# Review Gates

## Requirements Gate

Required approval from:
- Requirements Critic
- Product Manager
- UX Strategist, if user flows are affected

Must verify:
- Clear user value
- Testable acceptance criteria
- Edge cases included
- Non-goals defined
- Accessibility, security, performance, analytics, and observability requirements considered

## Architecture Gate

Required approval from:
- Frontend Architect
- Architecture Critic
- Solution Architect, for cross-system work

Must verify:
- Architecture fits requirements
- Contracts are defined
- Testing strategy exists
- Performance risks are known
- Security/privacy risks are known
- ADRs are recorded

## Implementation Gate

Required approval from:
- Code Reviewer
- Test Critic
- Accessibility Specialist, when UI changes
- AppSec, when auth/data/security-sensitive code changes

Must verify:
- Code follows conventions
- Tests are meaningful
- Accessibility is preserved
- Error/loading/empty states are handled
- No obvious security or performance regressions

## Release Gate

Required approval from:
- Release Gatekeeper
- QA Lead
- Security Critic, for security-sensitive releases
- Performance Engineer, for performance-sensitive releases
- Observability Agent

Must verify:
- CI green
- Required tests passed
- Known bugs triaged
- Rollback plan exists
- Source maps uploaded if needed
- Monitoring ready
- Feature flags configured if needed

